# 104 - §6 (.35): the compiler raises NO errors, so a body that cannot run is
# still compiled clean and simply never executed. Neither the undefined
# function nor the divide-by-zero inside it is ever reached, and the program
# completes normally. An engine that resolved names or folded constants at
# compile time would fail this program instead of running it.
--- source
if false {
  print nope(1 / 0);
}
print "clean";
--- expect
clean
